    "## 2.1. Audio Feature Extraction Methodology\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell defines the handcrafted acoustic feature extractor used in the StressID baseline experiments. The implementation is a lightly refactored version of the code provided in the official StressID repository. The main changes consist of clearer variable names, grouping the descriptors by feature family, moving the original VAD procedure to a separate helper function, and adding an explicit dimensionality check.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each waveform is loaded at its original sampling rate, processed with the StressID voice activity detection (VAD) routine, and converted into a fixed-length 140-dimensional representation. The representation concatenates the temporal means and standard deviations of MFCCs and their first- and second-order derivatives, spectral centroid, spectral bandwidth, spectral flatness, spectral contrast, spectral roll-off, Tonnetz, zero-crossing rate, and tempogram-ratio descriptors. The assertion at the end of the function verifies that the resulting vector preserves the expected dimensionality.\n",
    "\n",
    "<div align=\"center\">\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"img/diagrams/stressid_audio_feature_extraction_methodology_dark.svg\" alt=\"StressID corpus ingestion and filtering pipeline\" width=\"95%\"><br>\n",
    "<strong>Figure 2.1:</strong> Data-preparation pipeline used to derive <code>df_sid</code> from the StressID dataset structure.\n",
    "\n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "7b25620a-fe2e-4518-b6cc-d6647a6d56a9",
