    "## 2.2. Dataset-Level Feature Matrix Construction and Caching\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell applies the handcrafted feature extractor to every recording retained in the filtered StressID table, `df_sid`. Each successfully processed recording produces one 140-dimensional feature vector. These vectors are stacked into the feature matrix `X_audio`; the corresponding binary stress labels are stored in `y_audio`, and the subject identifiers used for group-based evaluation are stored in `groups_audio`.\n",
