    "Files that cannot be processed are omitted from the resulting arrays and recorded in a failure summary. After extraction, the feature vectors, labels, and subject identifiers are stored together in a Parquet cache. A separate metadata file records the extraction timestamp, number of samples, feature dimensionality, class balance, and number of failed files.\n",
    "\n",
    "On later executions, the cached dataset can be loaded without repeating the audio-processing stage. During local execution, the user may choose whether to reuse the existing cache or recompute and overwrite it. In Colab, the cache is loaded automatically when available; if it is missing, execution stops because feature recomputation is disabled in that environment. When loading the cache, the feature columns are ordered according to their numeric indices before reconstructing `X_audio`."
