    "## 2.3. Baseline Evaluation Protocols\n",
    "\n",
    "This section defines the evaluation procedures used for the handcrafted StressID features. Two main protocols are considered. The first is aimed at reproducing the classification methodology released by the StressID authors, including their classifier families, class-imbalance treatment, train–test splitting procedure, and reported evaluation metrics. The second extends that methodology with subject-independent validation, ensuring that recordings from the same participant are never shared between training and test partitions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The distinction between these protocols is important. The official StressID evaluation estimates performance across repeated random recording-level splits, whereas the subject-independent protocol evaluates whether the models generalize to speakers who were not observed during training. Because the official repository does not provide a fully version-pinned classification environment and includes stochastic operations, the first protocol should be understood as a procedural reproduction rather than a guarantee of exact numerical identity with the published results."
   ]
  },
