    "### 2.3.1. Official StressID Baseline Reproduction\n",
    "\n",
    "This subsection reproduces the official StressID handcrafted-audio classification protocol using the feature matrix constructed in Section 2.2. The implementation is a refactored adaptation of the authors’ `classification_audio.ipynb` notebook and its auxiliary `make_classification.py` module. The original classifier configurations, ten random 80/20 train–test splits, training-only SMOTE resampling, iterative imputation, feature standardization, weighted F1-score, and balanced accuracy are preserved, while the code is reorganized to operate directly on `X_audio` and `y_audio` and to expose the results in a more structured form.\n",
    "\n",
    "The evaluated classifiers are a Random Forest with a maximum depth of 5, k-nearest neighbors with \\(k=3\\), an RBF-kernel support vector machine with `gamma=\"auto\"`, and an `MLPClassifier` with no hidden layers and a maximum of 5000 iterations. No feature-selection method is applied in this reproduction.\n",
    "\n",
    "The official repository does not provide a version-pinned environment for the classification experiments. Consequently, the classifier configurations and evaluation procedure are reproduced from the released source code, but exact numerical identity with the published results cannot be guaranteed across different software-library versions.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because the reproduction protocol requires repeated model fitting, its outputs may be stored and reused across notebook executions. When cached results are available, local execution allows the user to either reload them or rerun the experiment, whereas Colab loads the cached results automatically. The cache includes the per-run metrics, aggregated summary, predictions, confusion matrices, and the main experimental configuration so that previously generated results are not silently reused after relevant protocol changes."
