    "### 2.3.2. Subject-Independent Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "This subsection extends the official baseline by replacing recording-level random splits with a subject-independent evaluation protocol. Recordings from the same participant are assigned exclusively to either the training or test partition within each fold, preventing speaker overlap between both sets. This protocol provides a stricter estimate of generalization to previously unseen speakers.\n",
    "\n",
    "To isolate the effect of subject-independent partitioning, the classifier configurations, preprocessing operations, training-only SMOTE resampling, and evaluation metrics used in the procedural reproduction are retained. The principal methodological change is therefore the replacement of repeated random 80/20 splits with grouped cross-validation based on subject identity."
   ]
