   "source": [
    "The recording-level protocol is useful for assessing whether the local implementation is broadly consistent with the results reported by the StressID authors. The subject-independent protocol is more demanding because it evaluates generalization to speakers who were not observed during training. A substantial performance decrease under this protocol would suggest that part of the recording-level performance may depend on speaker-specific patterns rather than on stress-related cues that transfer reliably to unseen subjects."
   ]
