    "## 2.6. Tuned XGBoost Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "This section evaluates the XGBoost configuration selected by the Optuna optimization in Section 2.5. To make the results directly comparable with the handcrafted baselines, the tuned model is evaluated under the same two partitioning strategies defined in Section 2.3: ten random recording-level 80/20 splits and five-fold subject-independent GroupKFold.\n",
    "\n",
    "For every training partition, `scale_pos_weight` is recalculated using only the corresponding training labels. Weighted F1-score and balanced accuracy are then computed on the untouched evaluation partition. The complete fold- or repetition-level results are cached and exported, while the notebook displays compact mean ± standard-deviation summaries consistent with the preceding baseline tables.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because the XGBoost hyperparameters were selected using the same StressID dataset rather than through nested cross-validation or an independent development set, these scores should be interpreted as post-selection estimates. In particular, the subject-independent result is useful for comparison with the baseline models but does not constitute a fully independent estimate of generalization to unseen speakers."
   ]
