    "## 3.1. Wav2Vec Embedding Extraction Methodology\n",
    "\n",
    "This section defines the deep-audio feature extraction procedure adapted from the official StressID implementation. Each recording is first loaded as a mono waveform and processed with the same StressID voice-activity-detection routine used in the handcrafted-feature pipeline.\n",
    "\n",
    "The speech segment is then passed through the pretrained Fairseq wav2vec model. Following the original StressID code, the model output is obtained by applying the model's `feature_extractor` and `feature_aggregator`. The resulting representation preserves the temporal dimension.\n",
    "\n",
    "For classifier-based experiments, temporal mean and standard-deviation statistics are computed over the aggregated wav2vec representation and concatenated into a fixed-length embedding. This reproduces the aggregation strategy used by the StressID authors when exporting deep features for classification.\n",
    "\n",
    "The original function name `DeepAudioFeatures` is preserved to maintain traceability with the reference implementation. The additional `DeepAudioEmbedding` helper is a notebook-level convenience function that encapsulates the mean–standard-deviation concatenation performed later in the original extraction script.\n",
    "\n",
    "Model loading is optional. When the Fairseq dependency or pretrained checkpoint is unavailable, the notebook remains usable through previously cached wav2vec embeddings."
   ]
