   "source": [
    "## 3.2. Dataset-Level Wav2Vec Embedding Construction and Caching\n",
    "\n",
    "This section builds the dataset-level wav2vec embedding matrix used in the deep-representation experiments. For each retained StressID recording, the `DeepAudioEmbedding` helper defined in Section 3.1 produces one fixed-length vector by concatenating the temporal mean and standard deviation of the aggregated wav2vec representation.\n",
    "\n",
    "The resulting embeddings are stacked into `X_w2v`, while the corresponding binary stress labels and participant identifiers are stored in `y_w2v` and `groups_w2v`. The extraction procedure preserves the same recording selection, StressID VAD preprocessing, and Fairseq wav2vec representation used in the preceding methodology section.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because wav2vec extraction is computationally expensive and depends on the local Fairseq checkpoint, the complete embedding dataset is cached. Cache metadata records the source dataset, embedding dimensionality, checkpoint identity, extraction timestamp, and relevant configuration so that incompatible cached representations are not reused silently.\n",
