   "source": [
    "## 3.3. Baseline Evaluation on Wav2Vec Embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "This section evaluates the fixed-length wav2vec embeddings using the same classical classifiers and validation protocols applied to the handcrafted representation in Section 2.3. This follows the StressID classical-classification formulation, in which the temporal mean and standard deviation of the wav2vec representation constitute an alternative feature set to the handcrafted acoustic descriptors.\n",
    "\n",
    "To isolate the effect of the representation, the classifier configurations, preprocessing, training-only SMOTE resampling, and evaluation metrics are kept unchanged. The only difference is the input feature matrix: `X_w2v` replaces the 140-dimensional handcrafted representation.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two evaluation protocols are considered. First, ten random recording-level 80/20 splits reproduce the partitioning strategy used in the released StressID classical baseline. Second, five-fold GroupKFold provides the subject-independent extension introduced in Section 2.3.2. Weighted F1-score and balanced accuracy are reported as mean ± sample standard deviation."
   ]
