   "source": [
    "## 4.1. Recording-Level Results\n",
    "\n",
    "This section consolidates the recording-level results obtained throughout the notebook. The comparison includes the results reported by the StressID authors for the handcrafted baseline, the local procedural reproduction of those baselines, the Optuna-tuned XGBoost model trained on handcrafted features, and the classical classifiers evaluated on the wav2vec mean–standard-deviation representation.\n",
    "\n",
    "All local results correspond to recording-level evaluation and are summarized using weighted F1-score and balanced accuracy. For the reproduced StressID baselines and wav2vec models, the values represent the mean ± sample standard deviation across repeated random 80/20 splits. The tuned XGBoost result is reported using the corresponding recording-level evaluation defined in Section 2.6.\n",
    "\n",
    "The values reported by the StressID authors are included as reference means only. Although the released implementation labels its second metric as `accuracy`, the underlying helper computes balanced accuracy; the metric is therefore presented consistently as balanced accuracy throughout this notebook."
   ]
