   "source": [
    "## 4.2. Subject-Independent Results\n",
    "\n",
    "This section consolidates the subject-independent results obtained throughout the notebook. In this protocol, complete participants are assigned to individual folds, so recordings from the same speaker never appear in both training and evaluation partitions. This provides a stricter estimate of performance when models are applied to previously unseen speakers.\n",
    "\n",
    "Only local results are included because the reported StressID baseline values used in Section 4.1 were obtained with recording-level random splits rather than the subject-independent GroupKFold protocol introduced in this notebook.\n",
    "\n",
    "The comparison includes the handcrafted baseline classifiers, the Optuna-tuned XGBoost model trained on handcrafted features, and the classical classifiers evaluated on the wav2vec mean–standard-deviation representation. Weighted F1-score and balanced accuracy are reported as mean ± sample standard deviation across the five GroupKFold folds."
   ]
